    "recommendations": "With only a single access point serving the property, clearly marking the driveway entrance with visible address signage that can be read from both directions along the access road could significantly improve navigation response times and reduce delays during emergency operations. The length of the driveway and presence of perimeter fencing may limit responder maneuvering options, so identifying and communicating a designated turnaround or staging area near the main building and detached structure would support effective apparatus positioning. Dense vegetation along travel corridors may reduce visibility for approaching responders, and selectively managing growth closest to the driveway edges could enhance sightlines and access continuity."
